# armour/man/lamellar: lamellar on the man (LADDER-ARMOUR, STYLE_P2 25.2 / 25.3 / 27.4: the Jade T3, the finer cut of padded
# and leather): vertical 1x3 plates (lit plate pixels step 3, the seams between them a step down) laced by an accent
# line every third row (the cord: accent 2 lit, 1 in shadow); a steel gorget, a belt, a solid band hem.
# Medium weight: the civilian silhouette plus the mid skirt (lamellar_hang, scallops and tassels by `when`) and the shoulders (shared/pauldron_scale*).
# Finish regions: R the gorget's rim and the hem band, P the lit chest, G the chest socket, N the lowest lacing row, W a 2x2
# spot on the shadow side. Keys: rest idle run runl drawn swing lie in D U R L.
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h. Source: LADDER-ARMOUR's expand.py (fill: lamellar).
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i1, P5) the lacing courses solid cords, the plate courses smooth planes (the blind
# panel: "the red-dotted lamellar is noise").
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i2) only the cord under the gorget and the cord under the belt stay; the middle courses are plate, one big lit plane (the style lens: thin stripes look busy)
# (LADDER-ARMOUR polish i3) quieter: one lacing cord across the chest; below the belt plain lacquer (the panel: "red-dotted
# lamellar is noise", "a stack of orange bars").
use person
body man
role armour lamellar
layer torso
anchor neck
keys torso
z 2

